{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22173 - PROTEIN:5778",
  "verbalization": "Cyclotetracosane is implicated in the regulation of DO4 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from its interaction with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This enzyme is targeted by both Ginsenoside R10 and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, which in turn target DO4. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DO4 suggests a potential role for Cyclotetracosane in modulating signaling through these enzymes, possibly by influencing their activity or expression. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The involvement of different targets (LC-PTP and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide) highlights the complexity of the interaction network, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the specific role of Cyclotetracosane in this process.",
